# AGENTS.md

{{ description.rstrip('.') }}. Architecture, import layers and extension recipes: [CONTRIBUTING.md](CONTRIBUTING.md).

The general rules come from two Claude Code plugins that `.claude/settings.json` enables, `conventions` and `nuikit`:
a skill per area, the `conventions-reviewer` and `descriptions-judge` subagents, and hooks that run `check-protected`
before each edit, `check-comments` and `check-conventions` after it and `review-comments` before you hand back. Fix
what they report. If the plugins are missing, add their marketplace once per machine:
`/plugin marketplace add nuinashco/conventions`. This template's own rules are in `.claude/rules/` (layout, runs,
tests). Exceptions this repo accepts are under "Deviations" in CONTRIBUTING.md.

## Design first

Before adding a module, family, command or config group, post a plan of at most 10 lines and wait for approval:

- the domain and its layer in the import contract;
- the pure half that decides and the effectful half that acts;
- a new family, or a new item of an existing one;
- the config fields, with their defaults;
- the test files.

{% if example %}
New code copies the shape of the example domain: `signals/` is a family (`base.py`, one module per kind in `items/`,
mirrors in `configs/signal/`), `stats/` splits a pure `summary.py` from an effectful `report.py`, and `cli/run.py`
wires them. Delete the example once the first real family exists (CONTRIBUTING.md says how).

{% endif %}
## Commands

```bash
make setup        # uv sync + git hooks (pre-commit, commit-msg)
make check        # ruff, the conventions checks, import contracts, pyright, pytest: before every commit
make format       # ruff fixes + format
make configs      # regenerate configs/ after changing any config schema
{{ '%-17s' | format(cli ~ '-run') }} # one run; results in runs/<run_name>/
```

## Layout

- `src/{{ package }}/cli/`: one module per console script; the only place objects are wired together.
- `src/{{ package }}/config.py`: entry config schemas; `paths.py`: repository paths.
{% if example %}
- `src/{{ package }}/signals/`, `src/{{ package }}/stats/`: the example domains.
{% endif %}
- `configs/`: Hydra YAML. Files whose first lines say `# Generated by` mirror schemas: never edit them by hand.
  `configs/run.yaml` is the hand-written entry config: values for every run go there.
- `scripts/`: exploratory or one-time runnables, never imported; a script that is rerun becomes a `cli/` command.
- `tests/` mirrors `src/`; `tests/test_invariants.py` holds the repo-wide checks.

## Before committing

- Run the `conventions-reviewer` subagent after adding or moving modules, configs, tests, entry points or docs, and
  fix its MUST findings; run `descriptions-judge` after changing config fields, descriptions or YAML comments.
- Commits are one line, `type(scope): imperative subject`, without articles, body or trailers. Docs change in the
  same commit as the code.
